--TEST--
`Core\Mail\Preview::keptCss` lists every rule left in `<style>` in the order of the HTML: an at-rule, a pseudo-class, a pseudo-element and a rule that matched nothing; `unusedCss` lists only the kept rules with no `:` outside brackets
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Mail\Preview::keptCss, Core\Mail\Preview::unusedCss
// Two `<style>` elements. Each kept rule stays in the element it was written in.
Core\Mail\Preview $mail = Core\Mail::preview(html`<style>
p { margin: 0 }
@media (max-width: 600px) { p { margin: 4px } }
a:hover { color: red }
.missing { color: blue }
</style><style>
p::first-line { font-weight: bold }
[href="https://example.com/x"] { color: green }
[data-ogsc] p { color: white }
</style>
<p><a href="https://example.com/">Home</a></p>`);
foreach ($mail->keptCss() as string $rule) {
    echo "kept: ", $rule, "\n";
}
foreach ($mail->unusedCss() as string $rule) {
    echo "unused: ", $rule, "\n";
}
echo $mail->html(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
kept: @media (max-width: 600px) { p { margin: 4px } }
kept: a:hover { color: red; }
kept: .missing { color: blue; }
kept: p::first-line { font-weight: bold; }
kept: [href="https://example.com/x"] { color: green; }
kept: [data-ogsc] p { color: white; }
unused: .missing { color: blue; }
unused: [href="https://example.com/x"] { color: green; }
unused: [data-ogsc] p { color: white; }
<html><head><style>@media (max-width: 600px) { p { margin: 4px } }
a:hover { color: red; }
.missing { color: blue; }</style><style>p::first-line { font-weight: bold; }
[href="https://example.com/x"] { color: green; }
[data-ogsc] p { color: white; }</style>
</head><body><p style="margin: 0;"><a href="https://example.com/">Home</a></p></body></html>
